# LevelDB compendium packs are binary data. Git must not touch line endings
# anywhere inside them: a CRLF in CURRENT makes LevelDB look for a manifest
# file whose name ends in \r, which does not exist, and the pack silently
# fails to open. Only bites on a fresh clone with autocrlf on, which means
# it bites a collaborator rather than whoever committed it.
packs/*/** -text -diff
